<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1.The above Audited Financial Results have been reviewed by the Audit Committee &amp; approved by the Board in meeting held on 30.6.20 2.Figures of the previous period regrouped/rearranged wherever necessary to make them comparable with those of current period. 3.Figures of the Quarter(Q) ended 31.3.20 are balancing figures between Audited figures for the year endedon31.3.20 and yeartodate figures upto the Q ended on 31.12.19. 4.Above results are available on www.shrenik.co.in&amp;www.nseindia.com. 5.Board recommended dividend ofRe.0.20 per EquityShare(10%) of facevalue ofRs.2/-each for the FYended on31.3.20 subject to approval of shareholders. 6.Financial Results for all the periods prepared in accordance with Accounting Standards(AS) as prescribed by the ICAI. 7.As our Co. migrated fromSME to MainBoard ofNSE wef 2.8.19, IndAS will be applicable to our Co. from next FYi.e.20-21. 8.EPS is calculated asper AS20 considering the split up of equityshares and EPS is adjusted for all comparative periods presented. 9.Management identifies Paper-Trading as only Business Segment.10.Significant disruptions have taken place worldwide due to COVID-19 pandemic. COVID-19 is significantly impacting business operation of the companies, by way of interruption in Supply chain of goods purchased &amp; sold, closure/lock down of Warehouses &amp; branch offices etc. The Co.'s warehouses &amp; branch offices were shut due to nationwide lockdown. Most of the operations of Co. have resumed post lifting of lockdown as per directions &amp; guild line received from Central &amp; StateGovt &amp;Local Bodies. In assessing the recoverability of Co.¿s assets such as Trade receivable, Inventories &amp; Short Term Loans &amp; Advances etc. The Co. has considered internal &amp; external information upto the date of approval of these financial results. The Co. has performed sensitivity analysis on the assumptions used basis on the internal &amp; external information of future economic conditions &amp; expects to recover the carrying amt of the assets.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
